The calculator produces several key metrics that inform betting decisions. The total number of parlays indicates how many individual bets comprise the round robin bet. Total stake cost multiplies the per-parlay stake by the number of parlays generated, showing the complete investment required. Maximum potential payout displays the return if all parlays succeed, whilst profit figures subtract the total stake from potential winnings. The calculator also provides scenarios for partial wins, demonstrating returns when only some parlays succeed. These outputs enable bettors to assess risk versus reward before placing their round robin bet, comparing total cost against potential profit margins.
